+## Provenance gained, remaining gaps
+
+The collection description identifies the item as Scott's May 23, 2003 hearing slides under June 17, 2004 military background materials. That supports its archival association; it does not prove the scan is byte-equivalent to the deck projected in May, that particular commissioners received/read it, or when it entered the binder. Five listed scans are not proof that every presentation slide or enclosure survives. [Collection finding aid](https://archives.iu.edu/ead/VAB8595.xml).
+
+The linked item resolved to a **6,358-byte JSON manifest**, SHA-256 **4da45eb940c92814e6701345015892c8f2fbc7943621ab6b411e60300030db35**. Five declared image-service requests, each 1600 pixels wide, returned JPEG page-image derivatives, totaling **1,028,723 bytes**. Original responses remain unchanged in the verified media store. The initial web-tool access error and sandbox DNS failure are preserved separately; the network-enabled public request succeeded. These access observations are not historical evidence of withholding or alteration. No PDF-export challenge route was retried.
+
+Native PowerPoint/authoring file, revisions, approval/dispatch records and the February 23 revised timeline remain TODOs. The six-page Scott MFR **NAID2609763** remains unacquired; its catalog naming and the 23-page staff-note release are not silently equated. The actual FAA corrected written answer and recipient acknowledgment, signed administrative determination and recommendation-specific dispositions remain separate outstanding inputs. All five tracks and 18 broad original-record/test groups remain open.
+
+No native audio/log/clock test, event-time reconstruction or actor-knowledge finding was performed. The related copies are not independent corroboration of wrongdoing. Earlier sources and reports remain preserved; [exact text diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff). Raw images, full OCR, headers, personal/contact material, private case information and internal coordination are excluded from publication.
